{
  "reason": "The 0.7468 trusted accuracy confirms the MLP+GBDT blend works (consistent with historical ~0.74-0.75 success), but the current fixed-weight blend gives almost no lift over either model alone because both base learners consume the same target-encoded representation and make correlated errors. The initial plan's direction — a heterogeneous stack (TabM, HGB, ExtraTrees, LogisticRegression-on-one-hot) combined by a LogisticRegression meta-learner on OOF probabilities — is the right ceiling-breaker and stays task-faithful (accuracy, original labels, fresh-process reload). Historical failures warn that oversized models cause exit-code-152 OOM under 2 threads/4GB/600s and that TE-only changes to the GBDT encoder barely move accuracy, so this refinement keeps each base learner cheap (bounded tree counts, one-shot LR, existing TabM/HGB configs) and adds only the decorrelating branches + learned stacker, with per-fold encoder fit + artifact persistence preserved exactly as in the proven merged pipeline.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Add a new stateless LRMatrixEncoder class alongside GBDTFeatureEncoder that produces a dense matrix for the linear branch — one-hot for the low-cardinality nominal cats (time, coupon, expiration, gender, maritalStatus, education, income, and the coupon×time/coupon×expiration interaction keys), plus standardized numeric columns (age_num, income_num, education_num, time_hour, expiration_hours, distance_est, freq_sum, freq_per_distance, and the *_ord freq ordinals from FeatureEngineer._base). WHY: the initial plan's fourth model is a linear learner on a one-hot view, which supplies a monotone global bias component the tree/neural branches underuse; without a dedicated leakage-safe encoder the LR branch would either parse raw strings inside transform (forbidden) or double-fit. HOW: fit(df) builds per-column level lists (slot 0 reserved for unseen), stores a mean_/std_ vector from training rows only, and shape-conforms transform via a fixed feature_names_ ordering; missing numerics imputed with fit-time medians. Keep it picklable (plain dict/list state) and never fit inside transform. INTERFACE: preserve FeatureEngineer, GBDTFeatureEncoder, _read_features, load_train_data, load_predict_data, TE_SOURCES, and build_train_matrix/build_predict_matrix signatures; LRMatrixEncoder exposes fit(df)->self, transform(df)->np.ndarray, feature_names_, and is additive only.",
    "model_design": "WHAT: Add two additive factory functions beside build_model/build_hgb: build_extratrees(seed) returning an ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators≈500, max_features='sqrt', min_samples_leaf=10, n_jobs=2, random_state=seed) that consumes the existing GBDTFeatureEncoder matrix, and build_logreg(seed) returning a LogisticRegression(C≈0.5, max_iter=2000, class_weight='balanced', solver='liblinear', random_state=seed) that consumes the new LRMatrixEncoder matrix. Also add build_stacker(n_features, seed) returning LogisticRegression(C≈1.0, max_iter=2000, solver='liblinear') used as the meta-learner on OOF probability vectors. WHY: the initial plan calls for bagged trees (different bias from boosting) and a linear branch (different bias from both) so the stacker can extract complementary signal; historical exit-code-152 warns against oversizing, so tree count is bounded (~500), min_samples_leaf=10 keeps variance low on 8k rows, n_jobs=2 respects the CPU cap, and liblinear on the small one-hot matrix is cheap. Keep TabM, TabMRank1Block, MODEL_CONFIG, HGB_CONFIG, build_model, build_hgb, build_criterion, build_optimizer, predict_proba, predict_labels byte-for-byte unchanged so existing artifact reload logic still works. INTERFACE: all new factories are additive; the existing model function signatures and the TabM state_dict/config contract are untouched.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: In cmd_train, per outer fold fit all four base branches on outer-train rows only — the existing TabM (via _train_one_fold with per-tensor state_dict cloning, unchanged), HGB over GBDTFeatureEncoder (unchanged 2-seed bagging), a new ExtraTrees over the same GBDT matrix, and the new LRMatrixEncoder+LogisticRegression — and write each branch's predict_proba into its own OOF matrix (class-index-realigned to label_classes). After the 5-fold loop, build a stacker feature matrix by concatenating the four OOF probability vectors plus a small set of engineered scalars (distance_est, freq_sum, is_bar, is_coffee), fit build_stacker on OOF, and report the stacker's OOF accuracy as Final Validation Score. Persist a new stacker_ensemble.pkl carrying the four branch OOF accuracies, the stacker coef/intercept, the per-fold ExtraTrees models, per-fold LRMatrixEncoders + LR models, and the existing gbdt_ensemble.pkl/tabm_ensemble.pt/feature_engineer.pkl contents stay as-is (or gbdt bundle gains an 'extratrees_models' key if convenient — do not break existing keys). In cmd_predict, load every artifact, average each branch's probability across folds with class-index realignment, concatenate in the SAME column order used at train time, apply the saved stacker, argmax, and _restore_label. WHY: the initial plan's whole value is that a learned stacker down-weights the correlated MLP/HGB and uses ExtraTrees+LR for genuine diversity; historical success shows fold-safe fit + artifact persistence + fresh-process reload is the proven contract, and failures show that a fixed weight-blend (or a TE-only tweak) cannot break the ~0.75 plateau. Reserve time by keeping NUM_EPOCHS=40/PATIENCE=8 (already trimmed), keeping ExtraTrees at ~500 trees (seconds), and fitting the LR branch once per fold (fast); if the total pass approaches the 600s budget, reduce ExtraTrees to 300 trees — never grow TabM or HGB. HOW: mirror the existing per-fold loop structure (encoder fit only on feats.iloc[tr], transform on feats_va), use get_cv_splits(y, NUM_FOLDS=5, random_state=42) unchanged, and keep _ckpt_load/_restore_label helpers as-is. INTERFACE: preserve cmd_train(data_dir, model_dir) -> float (returns stacker OOF accuracy printed as Final Validation Score), cmd_predict(data_dir, model_dir, output_path) writing exactly row_id,prediction with row_id 0..N-1 in input order, and the argparse train/predict subcommands guarded by if __name__ == '__main__'."
  }
}
